# pgsql-secrets.env -- corporatetraveldc-pgsql's OWN credentials
# (install as /etc/corporatetraveldc/pgsql-secrets.env, mode 0600, owned by
# the service user, never committed -- the directory itself needs sudo to
# create files in). See docs/POSTGRES_MIGRATION.md.
#
# NEVER QUOTE ANY VALUE IN THIS FILE -- podman's --env-file parser bakes the
# quote characters into the value. Same rule, same reason, same enforcement
# (scripts/check-env-quoting.sh) as dispatch-secrets.env.template.
#
# This is a DEDICATED file, deliberately separate from dispatch-secrets.env:
# the postgres container only ever needs its own password, and giving it the
# whole dispatch-secrets.env would expose every SWIM/NWWS/API credential on
# the box to one more process for no reason.
#
# The value here MUST equal DISPATCH_PG_PASSWORD in dispatch-secrets.env --
# the app containers authenticate with that one. Generate once:
#   openssl rand -hex 24
# Changing it later means changing BOTH files and ALTER ROLE dispatch.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME
